    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0525" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3448</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Senate Committee on Foreign
                        Relations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hitchcock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-20">January 20, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I enclose herewith copy
                    of Senator Knox’s<anchor n="6" xml:id="d191-f1"/> resolution, declaring that the
                    purposes of the United States at the peace conferences should be confined to the
                    restitution, reparation, and guarantees against the German menaces to the peace
                    of our country. The committee will consider this resolution next Wednesday and I
                    would be pleased to know before that time whether you have any suggestions to
                    offer as to the wisdom of adopting the resolution.</p>
                <p>Yours truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. M. Hitchcock</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d191-a1.xml" xpointer="d191-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d191-f1" n="6" xml:id="d191-f1-content">
                <p>Senator Philander Knox of Pennsylvania.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
